  "body": "The MCP server (`camcraft-cli mcp`) lets an AI agent drive CamCraft, but the only user-facing mention is two sentences in `guide/posting.md` and `developers/commands.md`. The real guide is the `camcraft-mcp` skill in `.claude/skills/`, which users won't find. Add a guide page for it.\n\nCover:\n- what it is and what an agent can do with it (build a job, add tools and operations, generate, verify, post, undo), and that every MCP tool runs the same undoable commands as the GUI;\n- the two ways to run it:\n  - headless on stdio (`camcraft-cli mcp`);\n  - attached to the open app (`camcraft-ui --mcp-port <port>` plus `camcraft-cli mcp --connect 127.0.0.1:<port>`), so the user watches the agent work live;\n- setting it up in an MCP client (a generic `command`/`args` config example, without depending on one vendor's client);\n- the tool list by area (job, tools, operations, setups and WCS, picking, posting), generated from the server's own `tools/list`, or with a note on where to get the current list;\n- an example session: load a project, add a tool, add a pocket, generate, verify, post, with the calls and short answers;\n- safety: the agent's output is held to the same refusals as the GUI; posted G-code is still proved on the machine the usual way.\n\nDone means: an \"AI agents (MCP)\" page in the guide that a user can follow to connect an agent, with both run modes, a client config example, the tool list and an example session.\n",
